+| D69 | Conceptual topic answers are delivered by the same deterministic chat-trigger shape as command usage: caller-text decision, verbatim post-sanitize bundle composition, topic-over-command precedence, at most one help block per reply | The D68 topic corpus is served by a second deterministic delivery trigger in `ChatAgent.doHandle`, shaped exactly like D67's: the decision to deliver is made by deterministic code from the caller's own inbound text, before the LLM is called, and the model's tool elections never feed it. **Trigger.** One embed round-trip serves BOTH delivery probes — the caller's inbound text is embedded once and the same vector drives `CommandIntentIndex.lookupTopic` (the topic probe) and `CommandIntentIndex.lookupCommand` (the D67 command probe). The topic probe runs FIRST at the M1-649-pinned `TOPIC_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD` (0.60): unlike the command trigger there is no lower-threshold tool path to be conservative against — this trigger is the topic corpus's ONLY consumer — so the pinned starting value applies directly, with the same recalibrate-as-follow-up posture (the M1-619 pattern). No tier filter: topics are tier-flat by construction (D68). **Precedence.** A topic match SHORT-CIRCUITS the command probe — a caller whose question trips both a command intent and a topic wants the explanation, not a bare usage block — so at most ONE help block (of either kind) appears in any reply; the cap is structural (the command probe never runs on a topic match), not checked after the fact. **Composition.** The delivered block is the fixed bundle-localized header (`reply.chat.topic_delivery.header`) plus the topic's `topic.<slug>.answer` bundle value at the scope's `/lang`, VERBATIM: the probe returns a slug pointer only (match-not-assert, D66→D68), resolved in memory via `HelpTopicCorpus.byTargetRef`; a stale pointer that no longer resolves degrades to no block. The block is appended AFTER sanitize + translate — the second authorized post-sanitize accretion under the M1-663 amendment to security.md §LLM output sanitizer, qualifying on the same path-(a) grounds as the D67 usage block (both the emission decision and the composed bytes are deterministic end-to-end) — and passes through neither the sanitizer nor `TranslationPipeline` (D43 two-path rule). Post-sanitize delivery is NECESSARY, not stylistic: topics must name user-tier `CLOSED_LIST` commands (`/add-source`, `/follow-tag`, …) that the sanitizer redacts out of model-authored text, and a model paraphrase would defeat the curation the corpus exists for — so a model-elected topic path is forbidden (the M1-648 r2 lesson, carried from D67). **Below threshold** no block is delivered and the model's own answer stands, a deliberate consequence: there is no model-side topic tool and no do-not-guess guard for corpus misses; recall is the job of D68's intent-shaped matching. **Injection posture.** An attacker-injected instruction in retrieved post content cannot cause a topic (or command) block: delivery is decided from the caller's parsed text before the tool loop, and tool-loop state never reaches the decision. Recorded by M1-666. |
 
